      "description": "MKG534 Student Visa Compliance Officer - Careers at Middlesex University Skip to main content Home Login Register Jobs Home Current Vacancies How to Apply Contact Us FAQ Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Home Login Register More ▼ Home Login Register Careers at MDX Careers at Middlesex Jobs Home Current Vacancies How to Apply Contact Us FAQ More ▼ Student Visa Compliance Officer Job Details: Job Description We are looking for a dedicated Visa Compliance Officer to ensure the University meets its critical United Kingdom Visa & Immigration (UKVI) sponsorship duties. You will play a lead role in maintaining our sponsor licence and visa compliance amongst our international student visa-holder community You will coordinate key compliance activities, from admissions checks and new student registration to the ongoing monitoring of existing students. A central responsibility will be managing our student attendance and engagement monitoring processes and associated reporting obligations. We are seeking an experienced compliance professional with in-depth knowledge of UKVI Student Route regulations. You are meticulous, proactive, and possess strong leadership skills to develop robust processes and guide university staff. Experience in a Higher Education setting or relevant regulatory/compliance environment is essential. For enquiries about the post, please contact Manesh Hanj, Student Visa Compliance Manager: m.hanj@mdx.ac.uk Middlesex is committed to fostering an inclusive working environment. We encourage applications from underrepresented groups including people from Black, Asian and minority ethnic groups, disabled people, LGBTQ+ people, women, and gender non-conforming individua